(Regression test: comparisons involving NaN used raw ucomisd flags, so NaN was considered less than, equal to, and not-not-equal to ordinary numbers.)
A float called nan is 0.0 divide 0.0.
If nan is less than 1.0 then, Print "lt1". Otherwise, Print "lt0".
If nan is less than or equal to 1.0 then, Print "le1". Otherwise, Print "le0".
If nan is greater than 1.0 then, Print "gt1". Otherwise, Print "gt0".
If nan is greater than or equal to 1.0 then, Print "ge1". Otherwise, Print "ge0".
If nan is equal to 1.0 then, Print "eq1". Otherwise, Print "eq0".
If nan is not equal to 1.0 then, Print "ne1". Otherwise, Print "ne0".
